    "transcript": "Test 5 Part 4. Ethics in Engineering. personal (31); bridges (32); wind (33); weight (34); sweetener (35); tank (36); trial (37); safety (38); pressure (39); licence (40).",
    "formContent": "<div class=\"ielts-form-container\"><div class=\"form-section\"><div class=\"form-title\" style=\"text-align:center;font-weight:700;\">Ethics in Engineering</div><p><strong>Ethics &ndash; principles relating to right and wrong conduct</strong></p><ul style=\"line-height:2;\"><li>at first, engineers saw ethics as a <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"31\" style=\"width:150px;text-align:center;\"> issue</li><li>attitudes changed because of three disasters involving the collapse of <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"32\" style=\"width:150px;text-align:center;\"></li></ul><p style=\"margin-left:20px;\">1876 &ndash; USA (metal fatigue)</p><p style=\"margin-left:20px;\">1879 &ndash; Scotland (the impact of <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"33\" style=\"width:150px;text-align:center;\"> on the structure was miscalculated)</p><p style=\"margin-left:20px;\">1907 &ndash; Canada (the structure could not support its own <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"34\" style=\"width:150px;text-align:center;\">)</p><p><strong>Boston Molasses Disaster</strong></p><ul style=\"line-height:2;\"><li>At the time, molasses was the main <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"35\" style=\"width:150px;text-align:center;\"> used in the USA</li><li>Boston company: collapse of a <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"36\" style=\"width:150px;text-align:center;\"> released 8 million litres of molasses</li><li>the wave of molasses destroyed buildings and the railway</li><li>local residents insisted on a <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"37\" style=\"width:150px;text-align:center;\"> of the molasses company</li></ul><p>Causes of the accident:</p><ul style=\"line-height:2;\"><li>insufficient <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"38\" style=\"width:150px;text-align:center;\"> check</li><li>the fermentation caused the rising of <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"39\" style=\"width:150px;text-align:center;\"></li></ul><p>Now, every engineer has to have a <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"40\" style=\"width:150px;text-align:center;\"></p></div></div>",
